# Cursor rules for Gamepad Mapper
#
# A thin pointer at the real sources of truth. Anything here that contradicts
# CLAUDE.md is wrong: CLAUDE.md wins.

# === Source of truth ===
Read CLAUDE.md at the repo root before any structural change. It defines the
three-thread model (Tk UI / mapping engine owning pygame + the injector / tray),
the injector ownership rules, the profile schema and the edge-case table.
README.md is for users.

# === Non-negotiables for this repo ===
- Runtime dependencies are fixed: pygame, pynput, pystray, Pillow, customtkinter.
- All pygame calls stay on the engine thread.
- Every synthetic key must be released on pause, profile switch, layout change,
  disconnect and exit. Release through the Injector, never the backend.
- Profiles are validated by model.normalize_profile; tracked profiles/*.json must
  match app/defaults.py.
- Keep 100% of existing behaviour unless the change says otherwise; every PR
  description has a "Repo-specific risks / edge-cases" section ("None observed"
  is fine).

# === Checks before proposing a commit ===
ruff check .
python -m pytest --cov

# === Conventional Commits ===
feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore, ci, perf, style, revert; optional scope;
breaking changes get "!" and a BREAKING CHANGE: footer. PR titles must conform
because they become the squash commit that release-please reads.

# === Other AI tools ===
See ai/AI_TEAM_PLAYBOOK.md.
